<BaseLayout title="Affiliate disclosure" description="How SelectVerdict discloses affiliate relationships and protects editorial independence."><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Affiliate disclosure' }]} /><PageIntro eyebrow="Transparency" title="Affiliate disclosure" description="SelectVerdict may earn compensation from some links. That support does not buy a favorable conclusion." /><article class="section narrow prose"><h2>How affiliate links work</h2><p>If you follow a qualifying link and make a purchase, SelectVerdict may receive a commission from the provider, generally at no additional cost to you. Relevant commercial pages identify whether an affiliate relationship exists.</p><h2>What does not change</h2><p>Compensation does not determine our research conclusions, the tradeoffs we describe, or whether a product is included. We do not accept payment for fake ratings, testimonials, or undisclosed placement.</p><h2>Our disclosure standard</h2><p>We aim to place a clear disclosure where a reader can see it before acting on an affiliate link. An affiliate destination should be stored separately from the product's official website in our content data.</p><h2>Your choice</h2><p>You can visit a provider directly instead of using an affiliate link. The research remains available either way.</p></article></BaseLayout>
